# Real values, at any depth and under any suffix - `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.production`. The
# committed templates are the two `.env.example` files and nothing else: this repository is public,
# and a secret published once stays published whatever a later commit does.
.env*
!.env.example
*.local
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
.claude/settings.local.json

# Playwright / Chrome DevTools MCP scratch output (snapshots, traces) - never part of the app.
.playwright-mcp/

# Blender writes these beside a .blend when a script saves one. The asset pipeline is
# script-in / GLB-out and never needs a .blend, so any that appear are scratch.
*.blend1
tools/blender/scratch/

# Cycles review renders and browser screenshots. Every asset script writes previews here so a
# model can be judged before it ships; the GLBs in application/public/world are the deliverable.
tools/blender/out/
tools/blender/preview.png
*-browser.png
/*.png

__pycache__/
*.pyc

tools/qa/out/

# Playwright matrix screenshots and reports.
tools/qa/out/

# The register of AzerothJS defects found while building this. It is notes ABOUT a dependency,
# not part of this product, and it is kept on the desktop rather than in the repository.
framework-bugs.md

